window.MONSTER_CHUNK_152 = [{"name":"Ravager Spawn","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"magical beast","init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":40,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":32,"ac_mods":"+8 Dex, +24 natural, -2 size","hp":405,"hd":"30d10+210 (+30)","hdvalue":30,"hp_mods":["regeneration 5 (epic-level weapons and artifacts)","vampiric healing"],"fort":25,"ref":27,"will":19,"defensive_abilities":["magic disruption (1 on d20)"],"dr":"15/epic","immunities":["energy drain"],"resists":[{"type":"death"},{"type":"energy","value":5}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"bite +37 (3d6+9/x3), 2 claws +37 (1d12+9/18-20)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","strength":28,"dexterity":26,"constitution":24,"intelligence":5,"wisdom":25,"charisma":18,"baseatk":30,"cmb":41,"cmd":59,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Lunge"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Fly)"},{"feat":"Snatch"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Wingover"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":22},{"skill":"Perception","value":18}],"sq":[{"type":"form-shifting"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","brood (2-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"With a crack and boom, this creature spreads a pair of great leathery wings over 50 ft. in span. Its body is lean and covered with rippling muscle beneath a thick, leathery crimson hide. Its claws and teeth are black, as are its eyes.","group":"Ravager","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Death Resistance","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn possesses an innate resistance to effects that would kill or permanently incapacitate it, including petrification and imprisonment. Against such effects it is considered to automatically make any required saving throws."},{"type":"Energy Resistance","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn possesses energy resistance against all forms of energy attack (fire, cold, electricity, acid, and sonic)."},{"type":"Form-Shifting","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn can physically alter its physiology to take on one of the three listed forms: the crawler, the brawler, or the flier. Doing so takes one minute, and during this period it cannot take any other actions, though it isn't considered helpless."},{"type":"Magic Disruption","kind":"Su","details":"Every time a Ravager spawn comes into contact with a spell or spell-like or supernatural effect, there is a chance as indicated above that the magic doesn't affect it. In the case of ongoing effects, a new check is made each round."},{"type":"Regeneration","kind":"Ex","details":"A Ravager spawn treats all damage as subdual, except damage from epic-level weapons and artifacts."},{"type":"Vampiric Healing","kind":"Su","details":"Whenever a Ravager spawn hits with a melee attack, it is healed hit points equal to half the damage it inflicts on its opponent. This ability cannot heal it above its natural maximum hit points. This ability extends to its trample special attack, where applicable."}],"description":"The Ravager was created eons ago by a primeval race of beings who believed in the unity of three forces: body, mind, and spirit. In their ongoing war with another race of savages, they created several weapons of terrible power. The greatest of these is the living beast known only as the Ravager.\n\nThis beast was given incredible vitality, and the power to manipulate its own body to assume a form most advantageous to it: a crawling weasel-like form that can burrow, a hulking apelike humanoid form with greater reach and strength, and a winged form to allow it greater mobility and agility.\n\nAfter being used once or twice on the battlefield, those who created it realized its awesome danger and contained it in the strongest prison they could devise, suspended in time until it would once again be needed.\n\nHowever, due to the subsequent influence of Orcus near the vault where the Ravager was contained, the wards were damaged, and a taint of evil infected its quarantine. This has resulted in it reproducing asexually, and has granted the ravager an astonishing capacity for growth. For every week that it lives, it permanently gains 1 hit die. There is no known limit to how far this advancement can go before it either devastates the planet it lives on or collapses under its own weight.","credit":"Originally appearing in Rappan Athuk Reloaded (© Necromancer Games, 2006)"},{"name":"Slag Worm","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"N","size":"Gargantuan","type":"outsider","subtypes":["earth","elemental","extraplanar","fire"],"init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["intense heat (10 ft., DC 30, 4d6 fire)"],"ac":36,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":34,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +28 natural, -4 size","hp":348,"hd":"24d10+192 (+24)","hdvalue":24,"fort":18,"ref":18,"will":20,"defensive_abilities":["fire absorption"],"dr":"15/adamantine","immunities":["fire","elemental traits"],"weaknesses":["susceptible to rust","vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"burrow","speed":30}],"melee":"bite +36 (6d10+22/19-20 plus grab)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"deafening roar"},{"type":"intense heat"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"4d6 plus 4d6 fire damage, AC 24, 34 hp"}],"strength":41,"dexterity":14,"constitution":26,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":19,"charisma":10,"baseatk":24,"cmb":43,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +4 vs. grapple","cmd":55,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":28},{"skill":"Bluff","value":27},{"skill":"Climb","value":39},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (dungeoneering)","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (engineering)","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":31},{"skill":"Perception","value":35},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":35},{"skill":"Survival","value":31}],"languages":["Ignan","Terran"],"environments":["any (Elemental Plane of Earth)","any (Elemental Plane of Fire)","any (Plane of Molten Skies)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This massive wormlike creature of burnt iron and glistening hematite grinds with the roar of the forge. Its fanged lamprey like mouth opens to reveal the molten fires burning in its gut.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Deafening Roar","kind":"Su","details":"Whenever a slag worm moves at least half of its speed in a single round it creates a grinding roar of metal on metal from its body. Creatures within 50 ft. that hear this grinding roar must succeed on a DC 30 Fortitude save or be deafened for 2d4 rounds. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Intense Heat","kind":"Ex","details":"A slag worm's body generates intense heat. Anything within 10 ft. of its body takes 4d6 points of fire damage each round. A DC 30 Fortitude save reduces the damage by half. Any weapon that strikes a slag worm must succeed on a DC 30 Fortitude save or melt into slag. (Magic weapons gain their enhancement bonus to their save.) A creature striking a slag worm with a natural attack or unarmed takes the same 4d6 points of damage each time an attack hits. The save DCs are Constitution-based."},{"type":"Fire Absorption","kind":"Ex","details":"Fire deals no damage to a slag worm. Instead, the slag worm absorbs the effect and heals 1 point of damage for each 3 points the effect would otherwise deal. If the amount of healing would cause the slag worm to exceed its full normal hit points, it gains any excess as temporary hit points."},{"type":"Susceptible to Rust","kind":"Ex","details":"Attacks that cause rusting (such as a rusting grasp spell or the touch of a rust monster) deal 2d6 points of damage to a slag worm."}],"description":"Slag worms burrow endlessly through the elemental Plane of Earth, Elemental Plane of Fire, and Plane of Molten Skies, occasionally forcing through weak points into the material planes where they burrow deep beneath the earth, devouring raw iron deposits to keep their internal furnaces burning. Because of this they have been known to devour entire companies of heavily armored dwarves and orcs, mistaking their gear for a new vein of naturally occurring iron salts.\n\nSlag worms average about 40 ft. long and weigh about 60,000 pounds, though specimens as large as 100 ft. or more have been rumored to exist. Its massive form radiates abysmal heat and when the worm opens its maw, fires can be seen burning and raging in its interior. They are intelligent creatures (more so than their appearance of a big dumb worm would lead one to believe) and can speak though they rarely choose to converse with other races.\n\nA slag worm erupts from the ground seeking to eat anything wearing iron, steel, or other metal armor or equipment. It attacks such creatures with a great ferocity, generally disregarding other enemies until the worm is heavily injured or forced away by magic."},{"name":"Sthenno","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":38,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":35,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +26 natural, -1 size","hp":225,"hd":"18d10+126","hdvalue":18,"hp_mods":["fast healing 5"],"fort":13,"ref":16,"will":17,"dr":"15/epic and good","immunities":["paralysis","polymorph","sleep","stunning"],"sr":31,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":50,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"2 claws +28 (2d6+10 plus grab), bite +28 (1d10+10), snake bite +26 (1d8+5 plus poison)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"petrifying gaze"},{"type":"poison"},{"type":"rend","details":"2 claws, 2d6+15"}],"strength":31,"dexterity":17,"constitution":24,"intelligence":22,"wisdom":22,"charisma":26,"baseatk":18,"cmb":29,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":42,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (snake bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":24},{"skill":"Bluff","value":29},{"skill":"Craft (alchemy)","value":27},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":29},{"skill":"Fly","value":18},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":29},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":27},{"skill":"Perception","value":27},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":27},{"skill":"Stealth","value":20},{"skill":"Survival","value":24}],"languages":["Abyssal","Aklo","Common","Draconic","Infernal","Terran (Euryale only)","Undercommon"],"sq":[{"type":"immortal"}],"environments":["any (Outer Planes)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair (Sthenno and Euryale)","troupe (true gorgon plus 2-8 medusa and 1-4 greater medusa)"],"treasure":"triple standard","description_visual":"This hideous creature appears to be almost twice as tall as a normal human. Its upper torso is that of a well proportioned human female with scaly flesh while its lower torso is that of a great black-scaled snake. Small black wings protrude from its back. Instead of hair, its head is covered with writhing, deadly asps. Its mouth is filled with razor-sharpened fangs.","group":"True Gorgon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Immortal","kind":"Ex","details":"Sthenno and Euryale are immortal and cannot die from natural causes. They are not subject to death from massive damage and are immune to death effects and disintegration. They don't age, and don't need to sleep, eat, or breathe."},{"type":"Petrifying Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"Turn to stone permanently, 30 ft., Fortitude save (DC 27 Sthenno, DC 29 Euryale) negates. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Bite-injury; save Fort DC 26 (Sthenno) or DC 28 (Euryale); frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d6 Strength; cure 1 save."}],"description":"Though the word gorgon is often associated with the deadly bull-like creature that turns a victim to stone with its breath weapon, the true gorgons are three sisters; Euryale, Sthenno, and Medusa. They are the daughters of the god Phorcys and the goddess Ceto. Euryale and Sthenno were born immortal and are hideous creatures with writing snakes for hair, brass claws, wings, and a gaze that can turn any living creature into stone. Phorcys tasked them with guarding the entrance to the Underworld.\n\nMedusa was born mortal and was very beautiful. Phorcys sent her to the Material Plane so all could gaze upon the beauty of his daughter.\n\nMedusa's beauty rivaled that of some of the goddesses, and some of them grew jealous of Medusa, particularly the goddess Athena. Her beauty also turned the heads of some of the gods, and when Poseidon seduced her in a temple to Athena, the goddess became enraged and changed the beautiful Medusa into a creature as hideous as her sisters. Poseidon turned from his love, never to return again. Medusa, enraged, fled into the desert and never came back to civilization.\n\nThe hero Perseus was tasked with killing the gorgon known as Medusa and bringing her head to King Polydectes as a wedding present. Using a magic shield given to him by the gods, he avoided Medusa's deadly gaze and severed her head. From her serpentine body sprang the children of Poseidon, creatures similar in appearance to their mother. These creatures escaped into the world and are called medusa.\n\nSthenno and Euryale long for their sister's return or their meeting with her in the Underworld. Yet being immortal, they cannot enter the Realm of the Dead. Thus, both know they will never see their beloved sibling again. Their cries are said to be audible on the wind as a high-pitched shrill akin to a bird's cry.\n\nBoth Sthenno and Euryale are 10 ft. tall and weigh around 600 pounds or more. Sthenno's eyes are blue; Euryale's eyes are copper.\n\nSthenno and Euryale rarely enter combat unless pressed or provoked.\n\nThey are both deadly combatants and use their claws, bite, snakes, and petrifying gaze with precision force. Sthenno enjoys \"collecting\" those she has turned to stone and even has a room in her lair where she displays them. Euryale simply smashes to rubble those she has petrified."},{"name":"Titivilus","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect good"},{"type":"detect magic"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":41,"ac_touch":28,"ac_flat_footed":34,"ac_mods":"+7 Dex, +13 natural, +11 profane","hp":275,"hd":"19d10+171","hdvalue":19,"hp_mods":["regeneration 10 (good, silver)"],"fort":15,"ref":20,"will":2,"dr":"15/good and silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":31,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"+3 silver wounding longsword +29 (1d8+10/19-20 plus 1 bleed) or fear touch +26 (fear)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"fear touch","details":"Will DC 32, fear spell CL 20th"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":29,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"bestow curse"},{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"confusion"},{"spell":"crushing despair"},{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"hypnotism"},{"spell":"illusory script"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"misdirection"},{"spell":"nondetection"},{"spell":"polymorph"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"tongues"},{"spell":"unholy aura"},{"spell":"ventriloquism"},{"spell":"whispering wind"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"feeblemind"},{"spell":"symbol of pain"},{"spell":"symbol of sleep"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 4d10 lemures or nupperibos, 1d4 bone devils or erinyes, 1d2 horned devils, or 1 pit fiend 100%"}]}],"strength":24,"dexterity":24,"constitution":28,"intelligence":28,"wisdom":26,"charisma":32,"baseatk":19,"cmb":13,"cmd":26,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Persuasive"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (confusion)"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":28},{"skill":"Bluff","value":40},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":38},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":29},{"skill":"Fly","value":29},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":37},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":28},{"skill":"Perception","value":34},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":34},{"skill":"Stealth","value":29},{"skill":"Survival","value":30}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Daemonic","Draconic","Giant","Goblin","Ignan","Infernal","Terran","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Hell)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Titivilus pls 2-4 erinyes or bearded devils)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This 6-foot tall creature resembles a satyr with a round hairless head, the lower torso of a goat, cloven feet, and clawed hands. Small black leathery wings sprout from his back. His eyes are the color of coal.","group":"Devil","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fear Touch","kind":"Su","details":"A creature that successfully saves cannot be affected again by Titivilus's fear touch for one day. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"Titivilus the Confuser serves Lord Dispater as messenger and chamberlain. He is a very evil and malign duke. His ability to manipulate others is legendary throughout the Hells, and it is because of this gift that Dispater allows him to attend infernal meetings where dukes are normally prohibited.\n\nTitivilus spends most of his days in his tower, Martyr's Curse, a large structure composed of blackened iron. When encountered away from his tower he usually has a small retinue of bearded devils or erinyes with him.\n\nTitivilus stands 6 ft. tall and weighs 220 pounds.\n\nTitivilus prefers to avoid combat, if possible. If pressed, he attacks with his spell-like abilities, seeking to sew confusion and disorder among his adversaries. In close combat, he uses his longsword, but usually summons other devils before such combat occurs. If facing imminent defeat, Titivilus summons other devils to cover his escape.","credit":"Titivilus originally appeared in Dragon #75 (© TSR/ Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and later in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission.","gear":"+3 silver wounding longsword"},{"name":"Wrath Dragon","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"NG","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["extraplanar","good"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"scent"}],"auras":["magic circle against evil (10 ft. radius)"],"ac":30,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +20 natural, -2 size","hp":465,"hd":"30d12+270","hdvalue":30,"fort":26,"ref":19,"will":23,"dr":"15/evil","immunities":["fire","poison","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":29,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +37 (2d8+15), 2 claws +37 (2d6+10), 2 wings +34 (1d8+5), tail slap +34 (2d6+15)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50 ft. cone, DC 34, 20d6 fire"},{"type":"channel positive energy","details":"8/day, 8d6, DC 22"},{"type":"crush"},{"type":"holy lance","details":"2/day, 7 rounds"},{"type":"might of the gods","details":"+15, 15 rounds/day"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":8,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":17,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon devas","details":"level 9, 1d2 astral devas, or 1d4 movanic or monadic devas, 100% chance"}]},{"frequency":"7/day","spells":[{"spell":"strength surge","details":"+7 bonus"},{"spell":"touch of good","details":"+7 bonus"}]}],"spellsprepared_caster":"cleric","spellsprepared_caster_level":15,"spellsprepared_concentration":24,"spellsprepared":[{"spell_level":8,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"antimagic field"},{"spell":"clenched fist","type":"domain"}]},{"spell_level":7,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"destruction"},{"spell":"holy word","type":"domain"},{"spell":"repulsion"}]},{"spell_level":6,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"banishment"},{"spell":"blade barrier"},{"spell":"heal"},{"spell":"stoneskin","type":"domain"}]},{"spell_level":5,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"atonement"},{"spell":"break enchantment"},{"spell":"dispel evil","type":"domain"},{"spell":"greater command"},{"spell":"plane shift"}]},{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"death ward"},{"spell":"dimensional anchor"},{"spell":"discern lies"},{"spell":"dismissal"},{"spell":"divine power"},{"spell":"holy smite","type":"domain"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"blindness/deafness"},{"spell":"invisibility purge"},{"spell":"magic vestment","type":"domain"},{"spell":"remove curse"},{"spell":"remove disease"},{"spell":"searing light"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"aid","type":"domain"},{"spell":"align weapon"},{"spell":"augury"},{"spell":"consecrate"},{"spell":"enthrall"},{"spell":"silence"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"bless"},{"spell":"command"},{"spell":"divine favor"},{"spell":"enlarge person","type":"domain"},{"spell":"remove fear"},{"spell":"sanctuary"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"guidance"},{"spell":"resistance"},{"spell":"virtue"}]}],"spelldomains":"Good, Strength","strength":31,"dexterity":14,"constitution":28,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":18,"charisma":20,"baseatk":30,"cmb":44,"cmd":56,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alignment Channel"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Snatch"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"},{"feat":"Turn Undead"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":38},{"skill":"Fly","value":27},{"skill":"Heal","value":37},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":38},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":36},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":36},{"skill":"Perception","value":37},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":37},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":38}],"languages":["Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Terran"],"environments":["any good-aligned plane"],"organizations":["solitary","band (1 wrath dragon plus 1d4 astral devas)"],"treasure":"triple standard","description_visual":"Beautiful and awesome to behold, this majestic dragon's skin glitters like precious metals and jewels, belying its unquestionable might and holy wrath.","group":"Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"A wrath dragon's breath weapon is a 50 ft. cone of holy fire. One-half of the damage is from divine force and isn't subject to fire resistance or fire immunity."},{"type":"Divine Power","kind":"Su","details":"A wrath dragon casts spells and channels positive energy as a good-aligned cleric. Its caster level is equal to half its Hit Dice. It has access to the Good and Strength domains and gains the domain power of each domain."}],"description":"These massive powerfully built specimens are formed from the ascension of slain good dragons into the heavenly orders. Given the opportunity to return, they serve as heralds of good-aligned deities sent to deliver divine judgment on infidels and sinners who have turned their back on the path of righteousness. A flight of wrath dragons over an offending city has often been cause to turn an entire civilization to prayer and piety. Wrath dragons never enter the Material Plane, inner planes, or other outer planes unless under orders from the deity they serve.\n\nWhen such orders are given, a wrath dragon completes its assignment to the best of its ability before returning to its home plane. A wrath dragon serves no one other than the deity that \"created\" it. It aids good-aligned creatures in time of need, but doesn't serve them or stay with them any longer than is required to give aid (unless its deific orders say otherwise). A wrath dragon never aids an evil creature under any circumstances, and if forced to do so by magical means, the dragon seeks atonement as soon as possible. A wrath dragon is 30 ft. long and weighs about 30,000 pounds. Its scales are silver or platinum and glitter under bright light.\n\nIts wings are silver-hued with a darker stripe running along the top portion. Its head, sitting atop its long serpentine neck, is long and angular and its eyes are seemingly made of sapphire. Two under-curved horns made of ivory jut from its head just behind its eyes. Wrath dragons start combat with use of their breath weapon and divine spells. They continue this tactic until pressed with missile fire, or magic that would force them to close in for melee attacks. In close combat, a wrath dragon attacks using a combination of its bite, claws, and spells. If pressed, or if the battle turns against it, a wrath dragon summons devas to its aid."},{"name":"Baaphel","cr":21,"xp":409600,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect good"},{"type":"detect magic"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":44,"ac_touch":19,"ac_flat_footed":37,"ac_mods":"+9 armor, +7 Dex, +11 natural, +7 profane","hp":270,"hd":"20d10+160","hdvalue":20,"hp_mods":["regeneration 10 (good, silver)"],"fort":14,"ref":19,"will":22,"dr":"15/good and silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":32,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30,"special":"40 ft. without armor"},{"type":"fly","speed":50,"special":"60 ft. without armor","maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"+3 axiomatic keen scythe +35 (2d4+19/19-20/x4) or fear touch +31 (fear)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"fear touch","details":"Will DC 27, fear spell, CL 20th"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":28,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"desecrate"},{"spell":"fire shield"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"tongues"},{"spell":"unholy aura"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"circle of death"},{"spell":"flesh to stone"},{"spell":"symbol of pain"},{"spell":"symbol of sleep"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 4d10 nupperibos, 2d6 bearded devils, bone devils or erinyes, or 1 ghaddar 100%"}]}],"strength":33,"dexterity":25,"constitution":27,"intelligence":26,"wisdom":26,"charisma":25,"baseatk":20,"cmb":31,"cmd":55,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (scythe)"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":28},{"skill":"Bluff","value":30},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":30},{"skill":"Disguise","value":27},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":30},{"skill":"Fly","value":34},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":28},{"skill":"Perception","value":35},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":35},{"skill":"Stealth","value":30},{"skill":"Survival","value":28}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Infernal","Terran","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Hell)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Baaphel plus 2-5 bearded devils, 1-2 barbed devils, or 1 pit fiend)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This dog-headed humanoid has grayish-brown, pale scarlet eyes, and two upright crimson horns. Two, large, black bat-like wings sprout from its shoulders. Its hands are clawed and its feet are blackened hooves. A forked crimson tail snakes behind it.","group":"Devil","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fear Touch","kind":"Su","details":"A creature that successfully saves cannot be affected again by Baaphel's fear touch for one day. The save DC is Charisma-based. Hell's Gleaning: Baaphel's unique weapon is a +3 axiomatic keen scythe."}],"description":"Baaphel is a grand duke in the service of Belial, leading 2 legions of bearded devils in battle for his lord. Baaphel is constantly scheming against the other dukes in Belial's service and takes every opportunity to discredit them in the eyes of their lord, though he never does this openly; it is always through lesser dukes and other devils that his machinations come to fruition. Baaphel yearns to be ruler of an entire plane and is waiting anxiously until the time comes that he can overthrow his lord.\n\nBaaphel makes his home in a great castle of basalt and iron called Evermore on Hell's fourth plane.\n\nBaaphel stands 7 ft. tall and weighs about 400 pounds.\n\nBaaphel attacks with Hell's Gleaning and spell-like abilities. He usually opens combat with flesh to stone, taking out the most able bodied attackers.\n\nBaaphel wears +3 chainmail and is rarely encountered without it.","gear":"Hell's Gleaning, +3 chainmail"},{"name":"Maphistal (Second of Orcus)","cr":21,"xp":409600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["unholy aura (DC 26)"],"ac":39,"ac_touch":24,"ac_flat_footed":32,"ac_mods":"+7 Dex, +15 natural, -1 size, +8 profane","hp":330,"hd":"20d10+220","hdvalue":20,"fort":25,"ref":13,"will":21,"dr":"20/cold iron and good","immunities":["electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":32,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":80,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"+3 unholy crushing heavy mace +35 (2d6+16 plus bone knit) or 2 claws +32 (1d6+13), bite +32 (1d8+13 plus disease)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":31,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"unholy aura"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"create undead"},{"spell":"desecrate"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"power word stun"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"telekinesis"},{"spell":"tongues","details":"self only"},{"spell":"unhallow"},{"spell":"unholy blight"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"circle of death"},{"spell":"fire storm"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 4d10 dretches, 1d4 hezrous, 1 nalfeshnee, 1 glabrezu, 1 marilith, or 1 balor 100%"},{"spell":"summon undead","details":"level 9, 3d10 zombies or skeletons, 2d6 ghouls, 2d4 ghasts, 1d6 wraiths, 1d6 wights, or 1d4 spectres 100%"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"create greater undead"}]}],"strength":36,"dexterity":25,"constitution":33,"intelligence":25,"wisdom":25,"charisma":26,"baseatk":20,"cmb":34,"cmd":59,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":35},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":31},{"skill":"Disguise","value":32},{"skill":"Fly","value":32},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (nobility)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":30},{"skill":"Perception","value":42},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":34},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":30},{"skill":"Stealth","value":26},{"skill":"Use Magical Device","value":31}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Goblin","Ignan","Infernal","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Maphistal plus 2-16 skeletons and zombies and 1-4 wights or 1-4 spectres and 1-8 wraiths)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"A stinking aura of death and decay lingers in the air around this feral-looking humanoid. Two great horns protrude upward from its oval head. Huge leathery, bat-like wings sprout from its shoulders, and its lower torso sports two massive legs that end in soot-colored hooves. Short, coarse black hair covers its entire body, except its face and clawed hands.","group":"Demon Lord","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Bone Knit","kind":"Su","details":"Each time a living creature is hit by a weapon wielded by Maphistal, it must succeed on a DC 25 Fortitude save or take 1d4 points of Dexterity damage as its bones fuse together. Creatures without bones or skeletal structures (such as oozes and plants) are immune to this effect."},{"type":"Disease","kind":"Ex","details":"Demon Fever: Bite-injury; save Fort DC 31; onset 1day, frequency 1 day, effect 1d6 Con damage and target must make a second Fort save or 1 point of the damage is Con drain instead, cure 2 consecutive saves. Vox: Maphistal's unique weapon is a +3 unholy crushing heavy mace. The crushing special quality crushes the skulls of those it strikes. Upon a successful critical hit, the weapon crushes the opponent's skull (if it has one) instantly killing the target. Some creatures, such as many aberrations and all oozes, have no skulls, others, such as golems and incorporeal undead, are not affected by the crushing special quality. Most other creatures, however, die when their skull is crushed."}],"description":"Maphistal is a lieutenant in the employ of Orcus, Demon Prince of the Undead. He makes his home on a stinking, smoldering Abyssal plane where he commands his troops from his great castle, Maalstege (The Keep of Bones—so called because it is believed to be constructed from the skeletal remains of those slain by Maphistal). He is loyal to no one but Orcus. He doesn't trust Sonechard, the General of Orcus's undead legions, and seeks to discredit him at any opportunity, though he doesn't do this openly for fear of rebellion by his troops or punishment by Orcus.\n\nHis machinations against Sonechard are primarily through his agents and spies in Sonechard's camps.\n\nMaphistal stands 9 ft. tall and weighs 700 pounds.\n\nMaphistal is rarely, if ever, encountered alone, and usually has a retinue of undead with him. When he enters combat, he usually opens with his spell-like abilities, immediately using his circle of death ability to affect as many targets as possible. In melee, he batters an opponent with his mace. An opponent whose skull is destroy (and who is therefore slain) or an opponent brought to Dexterity 0 (and not rescued by his comrades) is carried back to the Keep of Bones where it is transformed into an undead creature or becomes part of the Keep itself.","credit":"Maphistal first appeared in the Necromancer Games module R3 Rappan Athuk 3: The Lower Levels (©2002, Necromancer Games, Inc.).","gear":"Vox"},{"name":"Sonechard (General of Orcus)","cr":21,"xp":409600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":10,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["unholy aura (DC 27)","stench (20 ft., DC 32, nauseated, 10 rounds)"],"ac":46,"ac_touch":24,"ac_flat_footed":40,"ac_mods":"+6 Dex, +22 natural, -1 size, +9 profane","hp":385,"hd":"22d10+264","hdvalue":22,"fort":25,"ref":13,"will":21,"dr":"20/cold iron and good","immunities":["electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":32,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":80,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"+4 unholy wounding heavy pick +39 (1d8+17/19-20/x4 plus 1 bleed) or 2 claws +34 (1d8+13)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"control undead"},{"type":"undead master"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":32,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"unholy aura"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"create undead"},{"spell":"death knell"},{"spell":"desecrate"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"power word stun"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"telekinesis"},{"spell":"tongues","details":"self only"},{"spell":"unhallow"},{"spell":"unholy blight"},{"spell":"wall of fire"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"circle of death"},{"spell":"destruction"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 4d10 dretches, 1d4 hezrous, or 1 nalfeshnee, 1 glabrezu, 1 marilith, or 1 balor 100%"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 4d10 zombies or skeletons, 2d8 shadows, wights, or wraiths, 2d4 greater shadows or spectres, or 1d4 dread wraiths 100%"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"create greater undead"},{"spell":"fireball"}]}],"strength":37,"dexterity":23,"constitution":34,"intelligence":26,"wisdom":26,"charisma":28,"baseatk":22,"cmb":36,"cmd":61,"feats":[{"feat":"Bleeding Critical"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (heavy pick)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (heavy pick)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":17},{"skill":"Bluff","value":38},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":34},{"skill":"Disguise","value":35},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":28},{"skill":"Fly","value":22},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":34},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (nobility)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":33},{"skill":"Perception","value":41},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":33},{"skill":"Stealth","value":27},{"skill":"Survival","value":33}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Goblin","Ignan","Infernal","Terran","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Sonechard plus 1-4 wraiths or spectres, 2-16 shadows and 2-20 skeletons or zombies)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This ram-headed humanoid appears to be at least as twice as tall as a human and has leathery gray skin. Large, curved horns,-the left one broken off midway from its starting point-jut from its head. Two large bat-like wings spread from his shoulders. The creature's body is covered in thick, dark hair. Portions of the hair are torn away in areas revealing masses of battle-born scars and damage.","group":"Demon Lord","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Control Undead","kind":"Su","details":"This ability functions as the spell of the same name (CL 20th), except that Sonechard maintains control for 200 minutes. Sonechard can take control of undead creatures controlled by another creature whose caster level is 19 or less by making a successful opposed Charisma check against the opponent's Charisma check."},{"type":"Undead Master","kind":"Ex","details":"This ability allows Sonechard to create a maximum of 50 HD of undead with a single use of animate dead. If used in conjunction with desecrate, he can create 100 HD of undead with a single use. Fool's Errand: Sonechard's unique weapon is a +4 unholy wounding heavy pick."}],"description":"Sonechard is a General in the infernal armies of Orcus and serves him—at least to all onlookers—with unswerving loyalty. He has countless numbers of demons and undead at his command. Though his true loyalty lies only to himself, he would never openly refuse a request by Orcus nor challenge his position as Prince of the Undead. Should the day come when Orcus weakens, Sonechard plans to be there to claim what he believes is rightfully his.\n\nSonechard makes his home in a large castle called Chillhall that sits atop a plateau of scorched earth surrounded by a moat of blood. The walls are constructed of bone and sinew, and it is said that the souls of those who cross him are entombed within.\n\nSonechard stands 14 ft. tall and weighs about 3,500 pounds.\n\nSonechard is almost always encountered with a large number of demons or undead at his side. When he enters battle, he usually unleashes a fireball at his foes immediately, and then follows it up with a circle of death effect or a suggestion. Dying creatures are subjected to his death knell spell-like ability and then raised via animate dead.\n\nShould Sonechard find himself on the losing end of a battle, he doesn't hesitate to retreat, covering his escape with summoned or created undead and demons. A defeat isn't forgotten—or forgiven. He remembers his opponents, and sends his troops to exterminate them at first chance, bringing their carcasses to his keep where he grinds their remains into a fine powder and gives it to his servants to be used to spice up the keep's foodstuffs.\n\nSonechard's natural weapons, as well as any weapons he wields, are treated as chaotic-aligned and evil-aligned for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction.","gear":"Fool's Errand"},{"name":"Stygian Leviathan","cr":21,"xp":409600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Colossal","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["aquatic","extraplanar"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":28,"ac_touch":3,"ac_flat_footed":27,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +25 natural, -8 size","hp":522,"hd":"36d10+324","hdvalue":36,"fort":31,"ref":23,"will":16,"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +45 (4d6+24/19-20/x2 plus grab)","space":"70 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"capsize"},{"type":"Stygian poisoning"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"4d6+24 plus 2d6 acid plus Stygian poisoning, AC 22, hp 52"}],"strength":43,"dexterity":13,"constitution":28,"intelligence":4,"wisdom":14,"charisma":6,"baseatk":36,"cmb":60,"cmd":71,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Diehard"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Greater Overrun"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Overrun"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Staggering Critical"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":29},{"skill":"Swim","value":45}],"languages":["Common (cannot speak)"],"environments":["any (River Styx)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A gigantic whale, twice the size of ship surfaces. Its dark gray flesh contrasts hideously with the yellowish-white of its underbelly. It cuts through the water with a short, gray-mottled gray dorsal fin with a sharp curve. Its enormous mouth is lined with nearly 600 teeth of white or pale ivory color.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Capsize","kind":"Ex","details":"A Stygian leviathan can attempt to capsize a boat or ship by ramming it as a charge attack and making a CMB check. The DC of this check is 25, or the result of the captain's Profession (sailor) check, whichever is higher. For each size category the ship is larger than the leviathan's size, the leviathan takes a cumulative -10 penalty on this CMB check."},{"type":"Stygian Poisoning","kind":"Su","details":"The Stygian leviathan's stomach contains large quantities of water from the River Styx. Each round a swallowed opponent must succeed at a DC Swim or the swallowed creature slips underwater. Thereafter they must make a successful DC Fortitude save each round or be affected as by a feeblemind spell."}],"description":"The Stygian leviathan is the largest known creature swimming the River Styx. Very few inhabitants bother this monster and it has no known natural enemies.\n\nIt spends its time swimming throughout the Styx, gulping massive quantities of Stygian plants and aquatic life (such as fiendish octopi and fiendish krakens). Occasionally, it slips through a portal that leads to other planes—most often these portals carry it to the Material Plane. On the Material Plane, the Stygian leviathan doesn't deviate from its course—it simply swims about devouring whatever happens to get in its way. Some, on the other hand, actively hunt aquatic animals, preferring their flesh to the other more mundane food these monsters usually consume.\n\nThese beasts are solitary creatures and no more than a single leviathan has ever been encountered at one time (thankfully). Mating and reproduction cycles and methods are unknown and have never been documented.\n\nThese monsters are hunted by demons and devils for their flesh, which is used for food. Also, the teeth of dead Stygian leviathans are sometimes taken and fashioned into weapons of war.\n\nA Stygian leviathan attacks by simply swimming over its foes, opening its mouth, and swallowing them (and perhaps their ship if such a vessel is involved). Swallowed foes are drowned and digested."},{"name":"Vepar (Duke of Dagon)","cr":21,"xp":409600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["aquatic","chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":12,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["unholy aura (DC 27)"],"ac":37,"ac_touch":26,"ac_flat_footed":29,"ac_mods":"+8 Dex, +11 natural, -1 size, +9 profane","hp":363,"hd":"22d10+242","hdvalue":22,"fort":26,"ref":21,"will":15,"dr":"15/cold iron and good","immunities":["electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":32,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"+2 trident +35 (2d6+13/19-20) or 2 claws +33 (1d8+11 plus hypothermic touch)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":31,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"unholy aura"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"control water"},{"spell":"control weather"},{"spell":"control winds"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect law"},{"spell":"fear"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"polymorph","details":"self only"},{"spell":"water breathing","details":"others only"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"ice storm"},{"spell":"implosion"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 2d6 shrroths, 1d4 hezrous, 1d2 nalfeshnees or mariliths, or 1 balor 100%"}]}],"strength":33,"dexterity":26,"constitution":33,"intelligence":27,"wisdom":27,"charisma":29,"baseatk":22,"cmb":34,"cmd":61,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (trident)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (ice storm)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (trident)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":38},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":31},{"skill":"Disguise","value":35},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":30},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (geography)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":30},{"skill":"Perception","value":45},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":37},{"skill":"Stealth","value":29},{"skill":"Survival","value":30},{"skill":"Swim","value":22},{"skill":"Use Magical Device","value":31}],"languages":["Abyssal","Aquan","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Infernal","Undercommon","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"amphibious"}],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Vepar plus 2-5 shrroths)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This creature appears as a giant-sized merman with coppery-brown skin and silver scales. Its long black hair is braided and it carries a menacing-looking trident.","group":"Demon Lord","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Hypothermic Touch","kind":"Ex","details":"Those hit by Vepar's claw attack must make a successful DC 32 Fortitude save or be overcome with bone-numbing cold that deals 1d8 points of Dexterity damage. A successful save reduces the ability score damage by half. The save DC is Constitution-based. Demonbrand: Vepar's unique weapon is a Large +2 trident that can cast magic missiles seven times per day as a swift action (CL 15th). Additionally, the wielder can cast waves of fatigue once per day (CL 15th)."}],"description":"Vepar is an Abyssal duke in the service of Dagon, Prince of the Sea. He leads 29 battalions of shrroths in service to his master. He is a brooding particularly mortals (whose very existence he disdains). His loyalty to Dagon is questionable at best, for behind the scenes, Vepar is quietly amassing an army of demons to one day lead against his current lord. But for now, he waits and serves.\n\nVepar's citadel, Leviathan's Reach, is built into an underwater mountain range that sits several miles below the surface of his watery Abyssal home.\n\nThe citadel is guarded by scores of aquatic demons, fiendish merfolk, and fiendish tritons, as well as several hundred sahuagin led by a fiendish sahuagin 15th-level sorcerer named Anaunon. Most visitors (those that can actually reach it) avoid this place.\n\nVepar resembles a 12-foot tall merman. His upper torso is coppery brown while his lower torso and fins are silver and scaled. Vepar's hair is long and black, and he usually wears it tied back or braided. His eyes, usually blue in color, burn with a silvery fire when he is angered or excited. Under his hair, two small copper horns can be seen just above his eyes. Vepar's hands end in wicked claws with silvery nails.\n\nVepar relies on his trident, spell-like abilities, and ability to deal ability damage when combating foes. Before entering combat, he often raises a storm (using control weather or control winds) to herald his coming, though he is just as likely to attack from ambush or surprise as he is to \"announce\" his arrival. He enters combat with unholy aura active and follows it closely with ice storm.","gear":"Demonbrand"},{"name":"Baal (Duke of Hell)","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect good"},{"type":"detect magic"},{"type":"see invisibility"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"auras":["fear (20 ft., Will DC 29)"],"ac":43,"ac_touch":19,"ac_flat_footed":36,"ac_mods":"+9 armor, +7 Dex, +10 natural, -1 size, +8 profane","hp":333,"hd":"23d10+207","hdvalue":23,"hp_mods":["regeneration 10 (good, silver)"],"fort":16,"ref":20,"will":22,"dr":"15/good and silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":33,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30,"special":"40 ft. without armor"}],"melee":"+4 unholy morningstar +40 (2d6+17/19-20)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (20 ft. with morningstar)","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":29,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"comprehend languages"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"see invisibility"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"disguise self"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"inflict serious wounds"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"},{"spell":"produce flame"},{"spell":"pyrotechnics"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"tongues"},{"spell":"unhallow"},{"spell":"unholy aura"},{"spell":"wall of fire"},{"spell":"wind walk"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"fire storm"},{"spell":"symbol of stunning"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"shapechange"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 4d10 lemures or nupperibos, 2d4 barbed devils, bearded devils, or gorgons, 1d4 erinyes, or 1 ghaddar devil, horned devil, or pit fiend 100%"}]}],"strength":37,"dexterity":25,"constitution":29,"intelligence":25,"wisdom":25,"charisma":27,"baseatk":23,"cmb":37,"cmd":62,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (morningstar)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (morningstar)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":34},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":34},{"skill":"Disguise","value":34},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":26},{"skill":"Fly","value":24},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":34},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":33},{"skill":"Perception","value":37},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":37},{"skill":"Stealth","value":25},{"skill":"Survival","value":30}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Daemonic"],"environments":["any (Hell)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Baal plus 2-5 horned devils or 2-4 barbed devils)"],"treasure":"double standard Sheol: Baal's unique weapon is a Large +4 unholy morningstar. As a free action, the handle of Baal's morningstar can extend 10 ft., thus increasing his reach with this weapon. It can likewise retract to its normal length as a free action.","description_visual":"This diabolical-looking golden-skinned humanoid towers over you, dressed in battered bronze chainmail. It wields a large morningstar in its clawed hand as it stares at you. Its bovine head features large round eyes of black, a large nose, wolf-like upright ears, and a large mouth lined with razor-sharp teeth. Tiny forward-curving horns protrude from its forehead.","group":"Devil","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"Baal is a duke in the employ of Great Mammon and leads 5 legions of barbed devils in his service. Baal follows Lord Mammon's orders without question but secretly plans one day to wrest the throne from his master (who has become complacent as of late). For now, though, he waits and schemes.\n\nBaal stands 8 ft. tall and weighs 500 pounds.","credit":"Baal originally appeared as \"Bael\" in Dragon #75 (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and later in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission.","gear":"Sheol, +3 chainmail"},{"name":"Cherum","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Colossal","type":"aberration","subtypes":["fire"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."}],"auras":["fiery aura (40 ft., 6d6 fire, DC 36)"],"ac":37,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":32,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +1 dodge, +30 natural, -8 size","hp":450,"hd":"36d8+288","hdvalue":36,"hp_mods":["fast healing 15 when touching fire"],"fort":22,"ref":18,"will":24,"dr":"15/epic","immunities":["fire","poison"],"sr":33,"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"bite +33 (4d8+14/19-20 plus 2d6 fire plus grab), 2 claws +33 (3d6+14/19-20 plus 2d6 fire)","space":"30 ft.","reach":"30 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"swallow whole","details":"3d6+14 plus 2d6 fire damage, AC 25, 45 hp"}],"strength":39,"dexterity":18,"constitution":26,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":14,"charisma":12,"baseatk":27,"cmb":49,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. bull rush, grapple","cmd":64,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. bull rush","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Diehard"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Greater Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite, claw)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Intimidating Prowess"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":53},{"skill":"Bluff","value":20},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":54},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":22},{"skill":"Perception","value":45},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":24},{"skill":"Survival","value":23}],"languages":["Common","Giant"],"environments":["warm mountains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"double","description_visual":"This hairless mountain of slick raw burning flesh seems to constantly sizzle and ooze with the stench of burning fat. Two long meaty arms sprout from a hugely obese frame; its head appears to be little more than a bald sloping brow with black pits for eyes. Its maw splits open to reveal cavernous jaws, teeth glowing like huge red hot coals.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fast Healing","kind":"Ex","details":"A cherum heals only if it is touching a flame or lava pool that covers at least an area equal to its space (30-foot area)."}],"description":"The cherum is an abomination born of intense heat and crushing despair. Often making their homes in lava sprues, they are thought to be the rejected offspring of a fire deity (or at least the creation of said deity).\n\nAs such, they are often worshipped as divine beings by primitive folk who offer virgin sacrifices to appease the \"God of the Mountain.\" The cherum greedily devours such gifts, demanding more and more delicate flesh to feed its insatiable appetite. A cherum's deific background subjects it to fits of rage that can be felt for miles (especially when the cherum goes on a rampage and destroys the countryside).\n\nThough neutral by nature, cherum are often on decent terms with fire giants and other fire-based creatures that dwell near them. Though they don't trade with such creatures and rarely, if ever, aid them in time of need, they don't usually attack or demand homage from said creatures either. Cherum don't associate with dragons of any sort, especially red dragons for whom they have a great hatred.\n\nA cherum stands about 70 ft. tall and weighs well over 40,000 pounds.\n\nCherum are known to climb from a pool of molten magma, stretch forth their massive arms and devour everything in their grasp. They have little fear of dragons, demons, devils, or foolish adventurers who wander too close to their lair. They seek to grab and swallow everything smaller than themselves. If a fight goes against a cherum, it attempts to flee by diving into the nearest pool of lava and wait for its aggressors to leave as it heals.\n\nShould this fail, it fights on to the death."},{"name":"Deep Hunter Sea Serpent","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"LN","size":"Gargantuan","type":"dragon","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +1 dodge, +12 natural, -4 size","hp":324,"hd":"24d12+168","hdvalue":24,"fort":23,"ref":15,"will":12,"immunities":["paralysis and sleep","dragon traits"],"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +31 (2d8+15/19-20 plus poison and grab)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"2d8+15"},{"type":"poison"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"2d8+15 bludgeoning plus 1d8 acid damage, AC 15, 25 hp"}],"strength":31,"dexterity":13,"constitution":24,"intelligence":11,"wisdom":13,"charisma":12,"baseatk":24,"cmb":41,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":57,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Bleeding Critical"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Armor"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Spring Attack"},{"feat":"Swim-By Attack","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":13},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":14},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":9},{"skill":"Perception","value":24},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":14},{"skill":"Stealth","value":16},{"skill":"Survival","value":28},{"skill":"Swim","value":38}],"languages":["Aquan","Draconic"],"environments":["any aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"The serpent is about 60 ft. long and 10 ft. thick. Its body scales are smooth, each about the size of a large shield, and the entire serpent is deep green to jet black in color, with eyes a solid, nearly black red color.","group":"Sea Serpent","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Bite-injury; save Fort DC 29; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d6 Str; cure 2 consecutive saves. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"The immense deep hunter serpent lives in deep oceans, and delights in hunting down and killing the most fearsome creatures of the sea. The deep hunter lives on the ocean floor, usually near thermal vents and volcanic areas where it is relatively warm. However, when hunting it may be encountered just about anywhere at sea; its preferred prey are krakens and the largest whales, though it may attack any other fearsome sea predator—the more dangerous, the better.\n\nThe deep hunter sea serpent is seldom seen near the surface, as its prey tends to stick to deep waters. It doesn't initiate combat against creatures it sees as its inferiors, but if it does regard a creature as a threat, it uses stealth to surprise its prey when possible, and launches into a full-scale assault using all of its physical attacks to the best of its ability."},{"name":"Elemental Fire Dragon","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["elemental","extraplanar","fire"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["fiery aura (60 ft., DC 27, 2d8 fire)"],"ac":30,"ac_touch":14,"ac_flat_footed":24,"ac_mods":"+6 Dex, +16 natural, -2 size","hp":252,"hd":"24d10+120","hdvalue":24,"fort":13,"ref":20,"will":16,"dr":"10/epic and silver","immunities":["elemental traits","fire"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +32 (2d8+13 plus burn), 2 claws +32 (2d6+9 plus burn), 2 wings +29 (1d8+9 plus burn), tail slap +29 (2d6+13 plus burn)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50 ft. cone, DC 29, 16d10 fire"},{"type":"burn","details":"2d8, DC 27 rain of fire (100 ft. radius, DC 27, 2d8 fire)"}],"strength":28,"dexterity":23,"constitution":21,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":15,"charisma":12,"baseatk":24,"cmb":35,"cmd":51,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (breath weapon)"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Snatch"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":25},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":28},{"skill":"Perception","value":29},{"skill":"Survival","value":29}],"languages":["Common","Ignan"],"environments":["any (Plane of Fire)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This creature appears as a 30-foot long dragon composed of fire. Its eyes burn with a white-hot flame and flames lick the dragon's great mouth as it roars. As it flies overhead, its wings send sheets of flame roaring into the sky and crashing into the ground.","group":"Elemental Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"Afire elemental dragon's breath weapon is a 50 ft. cone of elemental fire."},{"type":"Fiery Aura","kind":"Ex","details":"Anyone within 60 ft. of an elemental fire dragon must succeed on a DC 27 Fortitude save or take 2d8 points of fire damage from the intense heat. The save DC is Constitution-based. Combustibles automatically catch fire if they contact an elemental fire dragon."},{"type":"Rain of Fire","kind":"Ex","details":"As a standard action, a hovering elemental fire dragon can rapidly beat its wings causing fire to rain down on an area in a 100-foot radius. Creatures within the area must succeed on a DC 27 Reflex save or take 2d8 points of fire damage as clothes catch fire or armor and weapons become searing hot. The damage continues for another 1d8 rounds after the attack or until the flames are extinguished. Combustibles in the area automatically catch on fire."}],"description":"One of the most feared creatures from the Plane of Fire is the dreaded elemental fire dragon. They make their homes in the heart of the many volcanoes that dot the elemental landscape. Composed entirely of flames, these magnificent creatures fear little and are respected and feared by those that have encountered them. Elemental fire dragons are malign, vicious, and thoroughly evil. They delight in killing and torturing others, especially magmin (whom they relish as a delicacy).\n\nThey often employ salamanders to aid them in their adventures, but once they have accomplished their goals, any surviving salamanders are usually devoured. Elemental fire dragons cannot enter water or any other nonflammable liquid, but they can fly or step over it. The typical elemental fire dragon is at least 30 ft. long. Elemental fire dragons are ruthless adversaries. They care nothing for treasure or anything of value. An elemental fire dragon attempts to annihilate its opponents using any means possible."},{"name":"Euryale","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":41,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":38,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +29 natural, -1 size","hp":270,"hd":"20d10+160","hdvalue":20,"hp_mods":["fast healing 5"],"fort":14,"ref":17,"will":19,"dr":"15/epic and good","immunities":["paralysis","polymorph","sleep","stunning"],"sr":33,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":50,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"2 claws +32 (2d6+12 plus grab), bite +32 (1d10+12), snake bite +30 (1d8+6 plus poison)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"petrifying gaze"},{"type":"poison"},{"type":"rend","details":"2 claws, 2d6+18"}],"strength":35,"dexterity":17,"constitution":26,"intelligence":24,"wisdom":24,"charisma":28,"baseatk":20,"cmb":33,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":46,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (snake bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":26},{"skill":"Bluff","value":32},{"skill":"Craft (alchemy)","value":30},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":32},{"skill":"Fly","value":20},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":32},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (dungeoneering)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":30},{"skill":"Perception","value":30},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":30},{"skill":"Stealth","value":22},{"skill":"Survival","value":27}],"languages":["Abyssal","Aklo","Common","Draconic","Infernal","Terran (Euryale only)","Undercommon"],"sq":[{"type":"immortal"}],"environments":["any (Outer Planes)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair (Sthenno and Euryale)","troupe (true gorgon plus 2-8 medusa and 1-4 greater medusa)"],"treasure":"triple standard","description_visual":"This hideous creature appears to be almost twice as tall as a normal human. Its upper torso is that of a well proportioned human female with scaly flesh while its lower torso is that of a great black-scaled snake. Small black wings protrude from its back. Instead of hair, its head is covered with writhing, deadly asps. Its mouth is filled with razor-sharpened fangs.","group":"True Gorgon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Immortal","kind":"Ex","details":"Sthenno and Euryale are immortal and cannot die from natural causes. They are not subject to death from massive damage and are immune to death effects and disintegration. They don't age, and don't need to sleep, eat, or breathe."},{"type":"Petrifying Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"Turn to stone permanently, 30 ft., Fortitude save (DC 27 Sthenno, DC 29 Euryale) negates. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Bite-injury; save Fort DC 26 (Sthenno) or DC 28 (Euryale); frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d6 Strength; cure 1 save."}],"description":"Though the word gorgon is often associated with the deadly bull-like creature that turns a victim to stone with its breath weapon, the true gorgons are three sisters; Euryale, Sthenno, and Medusa. They are the daughters of the god Phorcys and the goddess Ceto. Euryale and Sthenno were born immortal and are hideous creatures with writing snakes for hair, brass claws, wings, and a gaze that can turn any living creature into stone. Phorcys tasked them with guarding the entrance to the Underworld.\n\nMedusa was born mortal and was very beautiful. Phorcys sent her to the Material Plane so all could gaze upon the beauty of his daughter.\n\nMedusa's beauty rivaled that of some of the goddesses, and some of them grew jealous of Medusa, particularly the goddess Athena. Her beauty also turned the heads of some of the gods, and when Poseidon seduced her in a temple to Athena, the goddess became enraged and changed the beautiful Medusa into a creature as hideous as her sisters. Poseidon turned from his love, never to return again. Medusa, enraged, fled into the desert and never came back to civilization.\n\nThe hero Perseus was tasked with killing the gorgon known as Medusa and bringing her head to King Polydectes as a wedding present. Using a magic shield given to him by the gods, he avoided Medusa's deadly gaze and severed her head. From her serpentine body sprang the children of Poseidon, creatures similar in appearance to their mother. These creatures escaped into the world and are called medusa.\n\nSthenno and Euryale long for their sister's return or their meeting with her in the Underworld. Yet being immortal, they cannot enter the Realm of the Dead. Thus, both know they will never see their beloved sibling again. Their cries are said to be audible on the wind as a high-pitched shrill akin to a bird's cry.\n\nBoth Sthenno and Euryale are 10 ft. tall and weigh around 600 pounds or more. Sthenno's eyes are blue; Euryale's eyes are copper.\n\nSthenno and Euryale rarely enter combat unless pressed or provoked.\n\nThey are both deadly combatants and use their claws, bite, snakes, and petrifying gaze with precision force. Sthenno enjoys \"collecting\" those she has turned to stone and even has a room in her lair where she displays them. Euryale simply smashes to rubble those she has petrified."},{"name":"Gorson (The Blood Duke)","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":13,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect good"},{"type":"detect magic"},{"type":"see invisibility"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":44,"ac_touch":26,"ac_flat_footed":35,"ac_mods":"+9 Dex, +18 natural, -1 size, +8 profane","hp":372,"hd":"24d10+240","hdvalue":24,"hp_mods":["regeneration 10 (good, silver)"],"fort":18,"ref":23,"will":20,"dr":"15/good and silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":33,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"+3 wounding battleaxe +39 (2d6+15/19- 20/x3 plus 1 bleed), 2 forepaws +30 (2d8+6 plus grab)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"pounce"},{"type":"rake","details":"2 forepaws, 2d8+18"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":30,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"see invisibility"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"create undead"},{"spell":"desecrate"},{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"lightning bolt"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"},{"spell":"produce flame"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"tongues"},{"spell":"unhallow"},{"spell":"unholy aura"},{"spell":"wall of fire"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"symbol of stunning"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 2d10 lemures or nupperibos, 2d4 bearded devils, 1d4 bone devils, erinyes, or barbed devils, or 1 pit fiend 100%"}]}],"strength":35,"dexterity":29,"constitution":30,"intelligence":23,"wisdom":23,"charisma":27,"baseatk":24,"cmb":37,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":64,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Overrun"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (battleaxe)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (battleaxe)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":36},{"skill":"Bluff","value":35},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":35},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":33},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":35},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":30},{"skill":"Perception","value":33},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":33},{"skill":"Survival","value":33}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Goblin","Infernal","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Hell)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Gorson plus 1-3 barbed devils, bone devils or bearded devils, and 4-10 nupperibos)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This centaur-like creature is at least twice as long as a human and stands about 8 ft. tall. Its lower body is that of a great golden lion and its upper body is a coal-black humanoid with glaring crimson eyes. Its mane-like hair is thick, long, and dark brown, and the creature wears it draped over its broad shoulders and down its massive back. Its mouth is lined with sharpened fangs and its arms end in large, powerful hands. Splatters of dried and caked blood can be seen in the creature's mane and fur.","group":"Geryon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"The Blood Duke, Gorson, is a great lion-bodied humanoid that serves Great Mammon as 2nd general of his infernal army. Gorson leads 5 legions of barbed devils in service to his lord. Gorson is called \"The Lion\" for his ferocity in battle and his general appearance. He often takes the entrails of those he has slain and makes a necklace, wrapping it around his neck or entwining them in his bloody mane-like hair.\n\nGorson stands 8 ft. tall and is 12 ft. long. He weighs 1,200 pounds.\n\nGorson usually begins combat by leaping on a foe and rending it to pieces with his forepaws and rear claws. Those that survive this onslaught are subjected to a massive assault by his great battleaxe. Gorson attacks relentlessly and only stops when all foes are dead. Those that attempt to flee are run down and slaughtered.","gear":"+3 wounding battleaxe"},{"name":"Hutijin (Duke of Hell)","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect good"},{"type":"detect magic"},{"type":"see invisibility"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":43,"ac_touch":25,"ac_flat_footed":36,"ac_mods":"+7 Dex, +18 natural, -1 size, +9 profane","hp":297,"hd":"22d10+176","hdvalue":22,"hp_mods":["regeneration 10 (good, silver)"],"fort":15,"ref":20,"will":23,"dr":"20/good and silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":33,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"+4 unholy flaming burst trident +39 (2d6+17/19-20 plus 1d6 fire)","ranged":"net of snaring +28 (grapple)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"fear"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":28,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"see invisibility"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"create undead"},{"spell":"fireball"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"greater scrying"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"},{"spell":"mass hold monster"},{"spell":"polymorph"},{"spell":"power word stun"},{"spell":"produce flame"},{"spell":"ray of enfeeblement"},{"spell":"scorching ray"},{"spell":"shocking grasp"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"tongues"},{"spell":"trap the soul"},{"spell":"unhallow"},{"spell":"unholy aura"},{"spell":"unholy blight"},{"spell":"wall of fire"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"meteor swarm"},{"spell":"symbol of persuasion"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"heal"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 2d10 lemures, 2d4 ice devils or erinyes, 1d4 barbed devils, or 1d2 pit fiends 100%"}]}],"strength":37,"dexterity":24,"constitution":27,"intelligence":27,"wisdom":27,"charisma":29,"baseatk":22,"cmb":36,"cmd":62,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (trident)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (fireball)"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (trident)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":30},{"skill":"Bluff","value":34},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":34},{"skill":"Disguise","value":31},{"skill":"Fly","value":30},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":34},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":30},{"skill":"Perception","value":37},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":37},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":33},{"skill":"Stealth","value":28},{"skill":"Survival","value":33}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Goblin","Infernal","Sylvan","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Hell)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Hutijin plus 3-6 ice devils and 1-2 pit fiends)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This creature is at least twice as tall as a human and large bat-like wings protruding from its massive shoulders. A whip-like tail trails behind its scaled form. Its  hands and feet end in wicked-looking claws and its mouth is filled with sharpened teeth and two oversized fangs. Upward-curving horns project from its head. Its flesh is dark red.","group":"Devil","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fear","kind":"Su","details":"Hutijin can cause fear by speaking (this is a free action). Creatures within 30 ft. that hear his voice must succeed on a DC 30 Will save or be affected as though by a fear spell (CL 20th). A creature that successfully saves cannot be affected again by Hutijin's fear ability for one day. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"Hutijin is a loyal servant of Mephistopheles and commands 2 companies of pit fiends in the infernal armies of the eighth plane of Hell. Hutijin is a noble Mephistopheles' court and commands much respect from the other dukes and nobles. His battle prowess and strong demeanor command respect from the other dukes of Hell.\n\nHutijin stands 14 ft. tall and weighs 1,000 pounds.\n\nHutijin prefers to summon devils to deal with interlopers or adversaries, rather than waste time fighting them in melee. However, if pressed into combat, he fights with his trident, all the while peppering his foes with fireballs.","credit":"Hutijin originally appeared in Dragon #75 (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and later in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/ Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission.","gear":"+4 unholy flaming burst trident, net of snaring"},{"name":"Living Lake","cr":22,"xp":614400,"alignment":"N","size":"Colossal","type":"ooze","init":4,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":2,"ac_flat_footed":23,"ac_mods":"+21 natural, -8 size","hp":525,"hd":"30d8+390","hdvalue":30,"fort":24,"ref":12,"will":18,"immunities":["gaze attacks","visual effects","poison","sleep","paralysis","polymorph","stunning"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"4 (or more) slams +31 (4d6+17 plus grab)","space":"100 ft.","reach":"20 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"4d6+17"},{"type":"engulf","details":"4d6+17 bludgeoning, AC 20, 52 hp"},{"type":"trample","details":"4d6+25, DC 42"}],"spellsprepared_caster":"druid","spellsprepared_caster_level":20,"spellsprepared_concentration":36,"spellsprepared":[{"spell_level":9,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"antipathy"},{"spell":"mass cure critical wounds"},{"spell":"regenerate"},{"spell":"summon nature's ally IX"}]},{"spell_level":8,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"control plants"},{"spell":"earthquake"},{"spell":"sunburst"},{"spell":"whirlwind"}]},{"spell_level":7,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"animate plants"},{"spell":"control weather"},{"spell":"heal"},{"spell":"sunbeam"}]},{"spell_level":6,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"liveoak"},{"spell":"move earth"},{"spell":"stone tell"},{"spell":"summon nature's ally VI"}]},{"spell_level":5,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"animal growth"},{"spell":"baleful polymorph"},{"spell":"insect plague"},{"spell":"summon nature's ally V"},{"spell":"wall of thorns"}]},{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"blight"},{"spell":"command plants"},{"spell":"flame strike"},{"spell":"scrying"},{"spell":"summon nature's ally IV"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"call lightning"},{"spell":"dominate animal"},{"spell":"poison"},{"spell":"sleet storm"},{"spell":"water breathing"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"animal trance"},{"spell":"bull's strength"},{"spell":"flaming sphere"},{"spell":"heat metal"},{"spell":"hold animal"},{"spell":"lesser restoration"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"calm animals"},{"spell":"charm animal"},{"spell":"cure light wounds"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"produce flame"},{"spell":"summon nature's ally I"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"flare"},{"spell":"purify food and drink"},{"spell":"virtue"}]}],"strength":45,"dexterity":10,"constitution":35,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":22,"charisma":16,"baseatk":22,"cmb":47,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":57,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Empower Spell"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Armor"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack (slam)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell"},{"feat":"Spell Focus (conjuration)"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (slam)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":33},{"skill":"Perception","value":40},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":8},{"skill":"Stealth","value":14},{"skill":"Survival","value":38}],"languages":["Aquan","Common","Orc","Sylvan"],"environments":["any land"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"The lake's surface is calm and serene, and a cool morning mist rises from it. Suddenly, it is alive with activity as a massive pseudopod, towering dozens of ft. into the air, erupts like a cyclone.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Engulf","kind":"Ex","details":"A living lake that has grabbed an opponent can try to engulf the creature in its body. This ability functions as swallow whole, except for the following changes. An engulfed creature is trapped in the living lake's body, where the ooze inflicts automatic slam damage each round. In addition, an engulfed foe has no air to breathe and must hold its breath or risk drowning. A living lake can engulf 1 Gargantuan, 2 Huge, 8 Large, 16 Medium, 32 Small, 64 Tiny, 128 Diminutive, or 512 Fine creatures. If an engulfed creature cuts its way free, living lake simply flows together again and can still use its engulf attack."}],"description":"Hundreds of feet across, a living lake, also called an agrath-ogh in the language of the orcs, is an ooze of truly colossal proportions. The first living lake is said to have fallen from the heavens ages ago at a time so ancient that no eyes were around to witness its fall. The protoplasmic body of a living lake is fluid in nature and transparent in water, such that one of these creatures could remain unseen and unknown for centuries.\n\nUnlike most oozes, a living lake is a not a mindless blob of muck. It is intelligent, but it is also highly receptive to the thoughts and beliefs of any large group of intelligent creatures that live near it. A living lake can become a god—so to speak-because of the will of the creatures that worship it. Thus, it responds in a manner dictated by its own worshipers.\n\nThe god is created by the worshiper, instead of vice-versa. Unfortunately for the world, living lakes are generally found in hills and badlands—the very same environs favored by orcs. Living lakes worshiped by orcs are cruel, chaotic, destructive things, since those are the qualities most revered in orcish deities.\n\nOnce it has been ensconced as a god, a living lake uses its abilities to live up to the expectations of its worshipers. It can reward a tasty sacrifice with a life-giving rain, or punish insolence with a plague of insects.\n\nA living lake attacks by forming pseudopods from its oozy form and pummeling its opponents. A grabbed foe is constricted or engulfed in the creature's body, usually only released when it dies or falls unconscious.\n\nAgainst powerful opponents, or those that press the combat, the living lake mixes its spells with its natural attacks, usually summoning animals or animating plants to help it. A living lake usually forms at least one pseudopod per opponent it faces. It can form a maximum of one pseudopod per 3 Hit Dice it possesses."},{"name":"Caasimolar (Former President of Hell)","cr":23,"xp":819200,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":12,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect magic"},{"type":"detect thoughts"}],"ac":46,"ac_touch":28,"ac_flat_footed":38,"ac_mods":"+8 Dex, +18 natural, +10 profane","hp":391,"hd":"27d10+243","hdvalue":27,"hp_mods":["regeneration 5 (good, silver)"],"fort":20,"ref":25,"will":26,"dr":"15/good and silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":34,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"+3 cold iron good outsider bane quarterstaff +39 (1d6+15 plus inflict moderate wounds)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"fear"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":33,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"detect thoughts"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"cone of cold"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"invisibility","details":"self only"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"},{"spell":"polymorph"},{"spell":"tongues"},{"spell":"true seeing"},{"spell":"unholy aura"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"power word kill"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 2d4 bearded devils 100% or 1 pit fiend 80%"},{"spell":"wall of ice"}]}],"strength":27,"dexterity":26,"constitution":29,"intelligence":29,"wisdom":29,"charisma":30,"baseatk":27,"cmb":35,"cmd":63,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Craft Wondrous Item"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (cone of cold)"},{"feat":"Scribe Scroll"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (quarterstaff)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":35},{"skill":"Bluff","value":44},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":40},{"skill":"Disguise","value":44},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":40},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":36},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":39},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":36},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":39},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":36},{"skill":"Perception","value":43},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":43},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":36},{"skill":"Stealth","value":38},{"skill":"Survival","value":36}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Daemonic","Draconic","Giant","Goblin","Ignan","Infernal","Terran","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Infernus)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Caasimolar plus 1 pit fiend and 2-5 bearded devils)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"A wizened old man with a silver beard and balding head approaches. His eyes are ruby red and small rounded horns jut from his head, just above his eyes. His fingernails are ruby red, as is his long, snaky, thinly, forked tail. He is dressed in robes of purple, white, and amber.","group":"Devil","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fear","kind":"Su","details":"By speaking, Caasimolar induces fear in all creatures within 30 ft. that hear him. Creatures within the area must succeed on a DC 33 Will save or be affected as if by a fear spell (CL 20th). If the save is successful, that creature cannot be affected again by Caasimolar's fear for one day. Other devils are immune to the effect. The save DC is Charisma-based. Caasimolar's Iron Rod: This 6-foot long iron rod functions as a +3 cold iron good outsider bane quarterstaff. In addition, it has the following abilities: - 1/day-lightning bolt, range 100 ft., 15d6 electricity damage, Ref DC 25 for half - 3/day-slay living, touch (with rod), Fort DC 25 or die (3d6+20 damage if save succeeds) - Inflict moderate wounds each time a creature is hit with the rod, 2d8+10 damage; Will DC 25 for half."}],"description":"In the centuries when Lucifer ruled Hell, Caasimolar stood beside him as President. He was second in command behind only Lucifer himself.\n\nWhen the Great Uprising occurred Caasimolar was offered a position in Hell's new court, but he promptly replied by slaying the messenger and all the guards that had delivered the offer. Displeased with his answer, Asmodeus cast him out of Hell along with the rest of Lucifer's court when the Great Uprising was ended.\n\nCaasimolar is a cruel and malevolent creature and spends most of his time in his tower in Lucifer's basalt palace on the plane of Infernus. From his tower he enjoys watching the devils torture captured souls, particularly human souls. When not delighting himself in the torture of others, he is listening to reports from his vast network of spies he has encamped in the arch-devils' palaces in Hell. Though Caasimolar is no longer in Hell, little goes on there that he doesn't know about. His loyalty to Lucifer has never been in question and he keeps a close watch on those that offer advice, aid, information, or the like to his master.\n\nCaasimolar is never encountered alone except in his tower. When walking the halls of Malefacta (Lucifer's great palace) or tending to duties elsewhere in Infernus, he always has a retinue of 1 pit fiend and 2-5 bearded devils with him.\n\nWhen first engaged in battle, Caasimolar uses his fear effect against all within range that can hear him. When encountered with his personal retinue of devils, he prefers to let them fight, while he hangs back and peppers the enemy with slay living effects (from his rod) or cones of cold.\n\nIf his enemies force him into battle, he begins by releasing a slay living effect against who he deems to be the most powerful foe in the group. If this fails, he quickly unleashes a lightning bolt from his rod at the same target. If forced to fight close quarter, he relies on his rod's physical power as well as its spell-like effects, and he utilizes his spell-like abilities.\n\nIf the day is lost, Caasimolar summons devils to cover his escape before teleporting away to safety.","gear":"Caasimolar's iron rod"},{"name":"Cerberus","cr":23,"xp":819200,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["evil","extraplanar"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":40,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":32,"ac_mods":"+7 Dex, +1 dodge, +24 natural, -2 size","hp":465,"hd":"30d10+300","hdvalue":30,"hp_mods":["regeneration 10 (good)"],"fort":27,"ref":24,"will":20,"defensive_abilities":["immovable"],"dr":"15/epic and good","immunities":["death effects","disintegration"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"electricity","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":34,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60}],"melee":"3 bites +42 (4d10+13/19-20)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon"},{"type":"howl"},{"type":"petrifying gaze"}],"strength":36,"dexterity":24,"constitution":31,"intelligence":25,"wisdom":26,"charisma":24,"baseatk":30,"cmb":45,"cmd":63,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Intimidating Prowess"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Spring Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":40,"special":"+52 jumping"},{"skill":"Climb","value":46},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":50},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":37},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":37},{"skill":"Perception","value":45},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":42},{"skill":"Stealth","value":32},{"skill":"Survival","value":38,"special":"+46 when tracking by scent"}],"languages":["Abyssal","Auran","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Ignan","and Infernal"],"environments":["any (Hades)"],"organizations":["solitary (unique)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature is a giant-sized three-headed dog. Its fur is black and matted, and its eyes are crimson. Each mouth is dominated by long fangs, and each mouth drips foul-smelling saliva.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"As a standard action, once every 1d4 rounds, from his center head, Cerberus can spit a stream of poison to a range of 30 ft. Poison-contact; save Fort DC 35; onset immediate and 1minute; initial effect 2d8 Con; secondary effect 2d8 Con; cure 2 saves. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Howl","kind":"Su","details":"Any living creature within 600 ft. that hears Cerberus's howl must succeed on a DC 32 Will save or become panicked for 2d4 rounds. Whether or not the save is successful, an affected creature is immune to Cerberus's howl for 24 hours. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Petrifying Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"A creature meeting the gaze of all three heads must make a successful DC 35 Fortitude save or be turned to stone permanently. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Immovable","kind":"Ex","details":"Cerberus is immune to any extraordinary, spell-like, or supernatural effect or spell that would teleport him or move him from his current location. Only major deities can affect him with such magic."},{"type":"Immunities","kind":"Ex","details":"Cerberus is immune to death effects (such as slay living, finger of death, and so on) and disintegration."},{"type":"Regeneration","kind":"Ex","details":"Cerberus takes normal damage from good-aligned magic weapons, and from spells and effects with the good descriptor."}],"description":"The triple-headed Cerberus is the guardian of Hades. There is only one in existence and most creatures (both living and dead) are grateful for this fact. Cerberus is tasked with the duty of keeping dead souls in Hades. If a dead soul attempts to pass beyond the Gates of Hades and back into the land of the living, Cerberus attacks relentlessly until that soul returns to Hades. If slain, the soul is immediately devoured by Cerberus and is lost forever. Cerberus is also tasked with keeping living creatures out of the land of the dead (adventurers being what they are, they love to journey to Hades). Living creatures that attempt to move past Cerberus into Hades (through the main gates) are immediately attacked.\n\nCerberus is a 30-foot long black mastiff. He rarely chooses to communicate with creatures even though he speaks several languages.\n\nCerberus only attacks if a dead soul attempts to pass beyond the Gates of Hades into the land of the living or if a living creature attempts to enter the Realm of the Dead. Cerberus never willingly moves more than 60 ft. from the Gates and cannot be removed by any means, short of a god's magic.\n\nHe opens combat with his baneful howl and quickly follows with his breath weapon. Living creatures that don't retreat are subjected to his gaze attacks and bites. Cerberus attacks until all his opponents are dead or have retreated. The souls of those he kills are allowed to pass beyond the Gates and into Hades while Cerberus feasts on their body.\n\nIf slain, Cerberus's corpse melts into smoldering slime before fading away."}];
